  [1mOne thing you need to do:[0m [38;5;153mscripts/staging-ca.pem[39m doesn't exist yet, so [38;5;153msync_staging.py[39m will fail until you drop the
  staging CA there. Export it with:

  [38;5;153mopenssl s_client -showcerts -connect reports.staging.example:443 </dev/null \[39m
    [38;5;153m| openssl x509 -outform PEM > scripts/staging-ca.pem[39m

  Verify the fingerprint against whoever issued it before trusting it — grabbing a cert over the connection you're
  trying to secure only pins what's currently being served. If the cert is already on disk somewhere, point the env var
  at that path instead and skip the file.

